WEBVTT

00:10:27.542 --> 00:10:30.268
and you're trying
to get to the other side.

00:10:30.292 --> 00:10:31.559
Don't you agree with me

00:10:31.583 --> 00:10:34.976
that it would probably take
a really long time,

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:37.059
and you would probably get lost,

00:10:37.083 --> 00:10:39.726
if you had to go up and down
all of the mountains,

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:42.143
as opposed to if you just
drilled a flat tunnel

00:10:42.167 --> 00:10:44.601
that could go straight on through?

00:10:44.625 --> 00:10:47.309
Well it's the same thing
in our 5G devices.

00:10:47.333 --> 00:10:49.684
If we could remove this roughness,

00:10:49.708 --> 00:10:51.559
then we can send the 5G signal

00:10:51.583 --> 00:10:53.601
straight on through uninterrupted.

00:10:53.625 --> 00:10:54.875
Sounds pretty good, right?

00:10:55.792 --> 00:10:57.059
But hold on.

00:10:57.083 --> 00:10:59.559
Didn't I just tell you
that we needed that roughness

00:10:59.583 --> 00:11:00.976
to keep the device together?